  <name>Outlook for Linux</name>
  <summary>Unofficial Microsoft Outlook client for Linux</summary>
  <description>
    <p>Experience seamless integration with the Microsoft Outlook Web App in a standalone Electron application.</p>
    <p>This application is an unofficial client for Microsoft Outlook, providing a native desktop experience for Linux users with enhanced features like custom CSS, system notifications, and deep desktop integration.</p>
  </description>
  <url type="homepage">https://github.com/r4nmaru314/outlook-for-linux</url>
  <url type="help">https://github.com/r4nmaru314/outlook-for-linux/blob/main/KNOWN_ISSUES.md</url>
  <url type="bugtracker">https://github.com/r4nmaru314/outlook-for-linux/issues</url>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.r4nmaru.outlook_for_linux.desktop</launchable>
  <releases>
    <release version="1.0.3" date="2026-03-06">
      <description>
        <ul>
          <li>Initial release of Outlook for Linux fork based on Teams for Linux</li>
          <li>Adapted for Microsoft Outlook web application integration</li>
          <li>Full Electron wrapper with system notifications and tray integration</li>
          <li>Custom CSS support for Outlook customization</li>
          <li>Secure credential storage using Electron safeStorage API</li>
          <li>Cross-platform support for Linux, macOS, and Windows</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
  </releases>
  <developer_name>R4nmaru</developer_name>
